  "description": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "How new dynamics are influencing outbound mobility from Latin America’s largest market\n\nBrazil has long been one of the most significant student-sending countries in Latin America, with tens of thousands of students pursuing higher education abroad every year. As we move into 2025, several emerging trends are reshaping Brazilian students’ choices, creating both challenges and opportunities for education consultants and institutions worldwide.\n\nAt Collab International, we work closely with our exclusive partner Eduxplorers in Brazil, giving us first-hand insights into how this evolving market is changing. Below, we outline the key factors shaping demand and highlight how agencies and institutions can respond effectively.\n\n#1 Destination Shift: Traditional markets like the US and Canada remain strong, but Europe (Portugal, Spain, Ireland, Czechia) and Asia (Japan, South Korea) are gaining momentum.\n\n💲 Affordability Matters: Rising costs and currency fluctuations push families to explore lower-cost destinations."
    ],
